#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124301 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "69da2e7c-7ede-5966-8ff9-13bca51c0420" :question/math-academy-id "e-4813" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $\\mathcal{C}[-1,3]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-1,3] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ and its subset $A = \\big\\{ f \\in \\mathcal{C}[-1,3] \\: | \\: f(0)=-f(2) \\big\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under function addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of $\\mathcal{C}[-1,3]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of $\\mathcal{C}[-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x) \\in A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =-f(2)-g(2) \\\\  & =-(f(2)+g(2)) \\\\  & =-(f+g)(2),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means $f+g \\in A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x) \\in A$ and $k \\in \\mathbb{R},$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =kf(0) \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-f(2)) \\\\  & =-kf(2) \\\\  & =-(kf)(2),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means $kf \\in A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "7fed39de-7304-52a0-a94d-e55703175d7d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8233" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $\\text{M}_2(\\mathbb{R})$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $\\mathbb{R},$ and its subset $N$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is greater or equal to $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $N$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $N$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $N$ is a subspace of $\\text{M}_2(\\mathbb{R})$\n\nIV. $N$ is **not** a subspace of $\\text{M}_2(\\mathbb{R})$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $A_1$ and $A_2$ are two matrices from $N,$ then the sum of the elements on the main diagonal for each matrix is greater or equal to $0.$ Therefore, $A_1+A_2$ is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is greater or equal to $0.$ This matrix belongs to $N,$  and so $N$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $A$ is an element of $N,$ then the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is greater than or equal to $0.$ If we let $k=-1 \\in \\mathbb{R},$ then $kA$ is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is less than or equal to $0.$ This matrix does not belong to $N,$  and so $N$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $N$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "05151ae0-102c-5ce8-8bc6-082e22aa77d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8234" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $\\mathbb R_3[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3,$ and its subset $A = \\big\\{ at^3-bt \\: | \\: a,b \\in\\mathbb{R} \\big\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb R_3[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of $\\mathbb R_3[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)=a_1t^3-b_1t$ and $g(t)=a_2t^3-b_2t$ are two polynomials from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{3}-{b}_{1}t)+({a}_{2}{t}^{3}-{b}_{2}t) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{3}-({b}_{1}+{b}_{2})t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=at^3-bt \\in A$ and $k \\in \\mathbb{R},$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(a{t}^{3}-bt) \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{3}-(kb)t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ec3d76-867e-58df-a0fc-17b645b9779c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550370} {:answer/id #uuid "2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550442} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9e122e-367c-547e-8352-7b179ded0c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550649} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff1609f-3749-592a-a12b-50db0a8cc577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550781} {:answer/id #uuid "b04219c9-c7a8-5a0f-8c99-1a0abd96a1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2163c318-abcd-55be-97b4-9c32ae05ee00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550442} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6dae02d-3330-5599-b891-e70cc5b6da2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c7a58a4-6c9f-528f-bd18-00fe71c43a41" :question/math-academy-id "q-107100" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{4}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $4,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2},$ with $a,b\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{4}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{4}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{4}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}$ are two polynomials from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{4}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2})+({a}_{2}{t}^{4}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{4}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2}\\in A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(a{t}^{4}+b{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{4}+(kb){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550531} {:answer/id #uuid "6511a88a-c64f-5a4e-97b4-ca39d5115c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550611} {:answer/id #uuid "7e106959-31eb-50bf-a9a4-3a9026f280bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550680} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0ae82c-0963-5f9f-8291-b4680c80bd19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550917} {:answer/id #uuid "e348dd7c-e0f2-5cdc-b689-171bce7919c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4612c1ea-e787-5a0f-9afd-4cb22364e736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550531} :answer-field/id #uuid "f070b514-e12a-594a-9f0a-12adec04946c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60c155e6-f24c-5a27-86a4-e2d2fb148ceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107105" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3,$ and its subset $B=\\{a{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct\\,|\\,a,b,c\\in Q\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\nIV. $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t$ are two polynomials from $B,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & =({a}_{1}{t}^{3}+{b}_{1}{t}^{2}+{c}_{1}t)+({a}_{2}{t}^{3}+{b}_{2}{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}t) \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{3}+({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}){t}^{2}+({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $B$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},\\,{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}$ are in $Q.$ So, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(t)={t}^{2}$ and $k=\\sqrt{2},$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B,$ because $\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af81d6e6-3cad-5c8a-99a9-13bc107158af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447854} {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855} :answer-field/id #uuid "31478e71-bb60-536e-8adc-4001942eec0d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7871ce40-048e-5347-b7c4-782324459d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447856} {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857} :answer-field/id #uuid "19481cce-f1a9-5f87-8a34-93aac01ae946" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5f3b98c-c4eb-5c6c-ace2-f7e5a2fd7de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447858} {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99ca2b0-1668-5738-9b06-76be8f1daed7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} {:answer/id #uuid "fc911407-1e5d-58b7-8982-c859119fe356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b988c1-5329-5cf2-9e2b-7bef7867ab8c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89286e95-724b-57e9-aee8-7d71e484cafb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107113" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8e680db-ef52-5417-81b7-6ffe9b4383d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447898} {:answer/id #uuid "19085411-2145-5329-9d1c-475729adfa8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e680db-ef52-5417-81b7-6ffe9b4383d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447898} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b1197ba-c177-572c-bb95-f33fa8ad5099" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82cf67a9-3d8f-5ef6-a855-bb498bf43588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447900} {:answer/id #uuid "ae64a3e8-8b17-5d18-800a-c83f9d6df476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cf67a9-3d8f-5ef6-a855-bb498bf43588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447900} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3c1736b-4604-5446-818c-f015abcb2042" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99d1af0d-a2b6-573e-97da-18a0ba798138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447902} {:answer/id #uuid "0672ccdf-f372-53ce-8a7f-559b6aa2d02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99d1af0d-a2b6-573e-97da-18a0ba798138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447902} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0fabf2-df84-53f3-93cc-284ded8c1cc6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c2fad8-37dd-5870-9bbb-1b36235bf7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447904} {:answer/id #uuid "164c2063-3e52-529b-8591-4a7fddde2578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "164c2063-3e52-529b-8591-4a7fddde2578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447905} :answer-field/id #uuid "2108e5a4-e8f2-5a2c-9c41-5db4f1dcbb80" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3ebe5cf-3b69-5829-b6a6-d075f8831709" :question/math-academy-id "q-107141" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $W$ containing all polynomials of degree greater than $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $W$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $W$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $W$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $W$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}+1$ and $g(x)=-{x}^{3}+1,$ then\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)={x}^{3}+1+(-{x}^{3})+1=2,\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial of degree zero. So, $W$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(x)={x}^{3}$ and $k=0,$ then\n\n$$\nkf(x)=0\\cdot {x}^{3}=0.\n$$\n\n \nSo, $W$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $W$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} {:answer/id #uuid "75058ef8-65b5-5339-9bcb-1c1175a9c585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} :answer-field/id #uuid "603a8296-6812-5aa0-acca-2e58013b4290" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aea5044e-ffdb-5981-9a0d-1e77af7bb0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453228} {:answer/id #uuid "5e12f28f-5d7e-5ae4-9e88-d666b37d25f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea5044e-ffdb-5981-9a0d-1e77af7bb0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453228} :answer-field/id #uuid "2086fc9f-b317-5fdc-9df7-fec846619a6b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73efe5e7-86d9-56bf-883f-fdf28547d599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453230} {:answer/id #uuid "a85494a0-51a8-59e6-96b9-be4532a22c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73efe5e7-86d9-56bf-883f-fdf28547d599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453230} :answer-field/id #uuid "a819ffc8-0ac7-5428-aa18-b902a7881f2c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94acce7b-7200-5224-a551-0f52dea34c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453232} {:answer/id #uuid "5cef8fe4-d2dc-5067-8776-abd7c9ca57d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cef8fe4-d2dc-5067-8776-abd7c9ca57d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453233} :answer-field/id #uuid "88425d2a-b4ad-54eb-89a3-3a3b986d9505" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecd1a414-f091-5cfd-86f0-d0c82f6d9564" :question/math-academy-id "q-107147" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $K$ containing all nonconstant functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $K$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $K$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $K$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- **IV.** $K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n\n*Hint: $f$ is a constant function if $f(x)=\\text{constant}$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, the functions $f(x)=x+2$ and $f(x)=-x-1$ are in $K$, however\n\n$$\n(f+g)(x)=1\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1]$ and hence $f+g$ is a constant function. \nSo, $K$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, the product of the scalar zero by any function is the constant function zero. So, $K$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $K$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4447b957-2375-59a0-96bd-2d2ebc48393a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448650} {:answer/id #uuid "6a597dc3-f6e6-5c9e-a5fe-30ce9734d2a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4447b957-2375-59a0-96bd-2d2ebc48393a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448650} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c2a72c8-1cc2-50de-9127-bdd136cefa73" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c88baea7-9653-5c3e-9967-1a718f5e0eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448652} {:answer/id #uuid "94c030b9-b10e-5d6b-9737-415501ed7eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c88baea7-9653-5c3e-9967-1a718f5e0eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448652} :answer-field/id #uuid "2986970d-e359-59a5-9629-989d67564fb4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73d8dfe2-d4ee-54e7-8bf1-a8761d383398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448654} {:answer/id #uuid "184c6510-dc27-5b70-91c2-e24f060b5412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d8dfe2-d4ee-54e7-8bf1-a8761d383398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448654} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb4a36c-0b85-560c-9856-e1d1d306e125" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88f28f75-f6ea-513f-9b82-da9104ef6ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448656} {:answer/id #uuid "26813b3c-666c-5171-9966-8908acac6a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26813b3c-666c-5171-9966-8908acac6a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448657} :answer-field/id #uuid "192a8576-5898-5b62-a232-0ece84e0fecc" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4e607a0-6afc-5179-8279-85636fe2408c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43769" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2,$ and its subset $B={{t}^{2}+at+b\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$\n- **IV.** $B$ is a **not** a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(t)=g(t)={t}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & ={t}^{2}+{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(t)={t}^{2}$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =2{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8536f8a6-1bfc-5275-95ca-8a1fda0afe28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123525} {:answer/id #uuid "b659c777-4549-54ab-9f1f-bae85db6256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123526} {:answer/id #uuid "5da722ba-7c66-52bf-862c-fc5ad59257b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123527} {:answer/id #uuid "64f059cc-f403-5120-b592-b5803d968b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} {:answer/id #uuid "79c277c4-a05b-5a16-ab06-0142128ff522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64f059cc-f403-5120-b592-b5803d968b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} :answer-field/id #uuid "856e0bc2-ed8c-5746-a814-6831d1a835e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "027d54ca-a5e1-5f8e-b0e8-aea8a3580062" :question/math-academy-id "q-43770" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a\\in R\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n\nII. $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nIV. $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b3a3727-45a2-5fb4-95ae-a91e8f4f3239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451353} {:answer/id #uuid "560e913c-ce8a-5991-9d57-1efe0344f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "560e913c-ce8a-5991-9d57-1efe0344f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354} :answer-field/id #uuid "7994875a-855a-584f-b0b1-e9adddf96e49" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71e555b-f6a2-5bfa-a969-f07e226574ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451355} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe4cba6-6e86-5be1-8135-57a663228532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe4cba6-6e86-5be1-8135-57a663228532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451356} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae639aa0-32cb-59c4-89fa-57a75c8e85c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d934afb8-4872-512d-b557-15198d1a48a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451357} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f2982f-15e7-58c5-94f1-438da460594b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f2982f-15e7-58c5-94f1-438da460594b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451358} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a8d921-2a8a-515d-b4dc-86f366326881" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc6f1bb2-59b1-5487-b01f-c8947e4f8b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451359} {:answer/id #uuid "ee66f17e-227c-5e22-9f23-dbee97ac1f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc6f1bb2-59b1-5487-b01f-c8947e4f8b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451359} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9876e54-bdbd-59af-a25c-ae629c2446e5" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ed6c488-d6f4-5c35-b1ec-2f3c2d68e465" :question/math-academy-id "q-43779" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-1,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-1,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[-1,1]\\,|\\,f(1)=f(-1)}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under function addition\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of $C[-1,1]$\n- **IV.** $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-1,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(1) & =f(1)+g(1) \\\\  & =f(-1)+g(-1) \\\\  & =(f+g)(-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(1) & =kf(1) \\\\  & =kf(-1) \\\\  & =(kf)(-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $B$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5477cd7b-f9c9-5c7f-a607-f368ecf237de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451937} {:answer/id #uuid "4356813c-3793-5eb3-9f96-9e5097fea019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5477cd7b-f9c9-5c7f-a607-f368ecf237de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451937} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dbfd750-72a7-524b-8bc7-6d10bf74a4d0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8894f4d-90d8-53b4-bc65-9af198753c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451939} {:answer/id #uuid "27e95ad7-d915-56b0-8295-2fc259ae000b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8894f4d-90d8-53b4-bc65-9af198753c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451939} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7269288-bc2a-5146-b1cc-8c0e8653330e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b47b1139-8b3d-5f7c-b65e-aa35843f713d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451941} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb558a0-c346-532f-9101-0ba693e2a378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b47b1139-8b3d-5f7c-b65e-aa35843f713d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451941} :answer-field/id #uuid "92326df0-69fd-5473-9063-f9fd81a501aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad63500-4f97-5dd3-82f7-7907ecb5913c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451943} {:answer/id #uuid "4bed21ac-7c48-54e9-8a98-bbbd3cb520d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bed21ac-7c48-54e9-8a98-bbbd3cb520d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451944} :answer-field/id #uuid "71941d3e-46d1-5c03-ad74-08aa7d83fff7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef92c245-5042-5dba-9942-02e46fcd2132" :question/math-academy-id "q-94612" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2,$ and its subset $B=\\{p(t)\\in {R}_{2}[t]\\,|\\,p(1)=2\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$\n\n- **IV.** $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(1)=g(1)=2,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1)+g(1) & =2+2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(1)=2$ and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(1) & =2\\cdot 2=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0633560a-9503-5656-8072-6bcc75a4445c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550386} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550721} {:answer/id #uuid "df76d186-e3ec-5f89-9781-557292058054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550976} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5175b1-31a1-53ab-8237-6c7fc548fae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551007} {:answer/id #uuid "fb99258c-ef45-5fe2-b87d-9b48445cde8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ac94541-a732-5a4d-b872-29df378de699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550721} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1d8442-a2da-505e-aaa8-1ed74221f3da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31d0899c-0442-5601-b2c5-58d91ebde08a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94616" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{5}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{5},$ where $a\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{5}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{5}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{5},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & ={a}_{1}{t}^{5}+{a}_{2}{t}^{5} \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{5},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{5}$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =ka{t}^{5} \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{5},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9082d0ca-6137-5774-b9e3-7f0e4a8c73a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451953} {:answer/id #uuid "8be89cec-384b-5bff-8e16-25e2f4a93c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be89cec-384b-5bff-8e16-25e2f4a93c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218645195