 :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451959} {:answer/id #uuid "770810e2-9b98-501c-b7d6-38738d90eb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b135c823-a7f2-5267-92f0-2062c99ce9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451959} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a8139b-28d0-5f8e-be9a-7298bbcbb11c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ffc0d2e-16d3-51e9-8958-0f5807298d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-94624" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $E$ containing all diagonal $2\\times 2$ matrices.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $E$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $E,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A$ is an element of $E,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a diagonal matrix. This matrix belongs to $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f077c77-0570-536a-a8a6-0a63cf4d87ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454146} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b59da7-192e-5638-a6d9-30b5ec427b19" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} {:answer/id #uuid "3146b088-175e-5e2a-8f28-d752332c1825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} :answer-field/id #uuid "a160776e-c9a6-54ab-ba04-03293503bfa9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6f3468-8a4e-525c-91f1-9eb0300f4e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} :answer-field/id #uuid "de85e3af-f485-549e-af6a-03e3f37ec071" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437f3bf2-f29e-5af5-aed6-837e31083c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454152} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153} :answer-field/id #uuid "82587102-0923-537e-9e88-86ad077d77a6" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02488e4e-8845-5c5e-a156-a562e8b67a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-94627" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $D={\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a<0}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $D$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $D,$ then  ${a}_{1}<0$ and ${a}_{2}<0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n is a matrix from $D,$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}<0.$ So, $D$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example,  if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $k=-1,$ then $A$ is an element of $D$ and $k\\in R,$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis *not* in  $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $D$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1642353f-4507-5ad2-b44d-dbb363c5619b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #e